From acf8a65be79d0757f592f33662aea0d272b744f0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Rhino <195818135+1rhino2@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 06:18:22 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] transfer: drop a pending read rewind when a new transfer
 starts

Curl_req_hard_reset() keeps the client reader stack when a rewind is
pending and only clears the flag afterwards, so when a redirect with a
request body fails before the follow-up request is set up, the readers
of the previous body stay installed into the next transfer on the same
easy handle. An upload over a protocol that uses the generic reader
(ftp, sftp, scp, file, tftp) then reads through the stale stack, and if
the postfields were replaced in between that memory is gone.

Clear a pending rewind and reset the readers in Curl_pretransfer(), a
new transfer never wants a rewind of the previous body.

Closes #23505

(cherry picked from commit acf8a65be79d0757f592f33662aea0d272b744f0)
---
 lib/transfer.c | 6 ++++++
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+)

diff --git a/lib/transfer.c b/lib/transfer.c
index 3f0f215..abc7623 100644
--- a/lib/transfer.c
+++ b/lib/transfer.c
@@ -590,6 +590,12 @@ CURLcode Curl_pretransfer(struct Curl_easy *data)
   }
 
   data->req.headerbytecount = 0;
+  /* a previous transfer on this handle may have ended with a rewind request
+   * still pending (a follow or auth retry that failed). This is a new
+   * transfer, so drop those readers now instead of letting a later upload
+   * read from them. */
+  data->req.rewind_read = FALSE;
+  Curl_client_reset(data);
   Curl_headers_cleanup(data);
   return result;
 }
